From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:09:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CUSTOM: worgen human form - stored human look, form swap,
 ZEPF block, barber (F-236)

- character_customizations 100-115 = the human form look (16-byte look: skin, face, hair style,
  hair colour, facial hair, eye/markings, jewellery, geoset slots); loaded with the other customizations
- Player::SetZepAlteredForm swaps the human look into PLAYER_BYTES / PLAYER_BYTES_2 / UNIT_FIELD_PADDING /
  OBJECT_FIELD_PADDING and sets bit 31 of OBJECT_FIELD_PADDING (jewellery now 7-bit) in one update tick
- SaveToDB, corpse and shapeshift model colour always use the native (worgen) look; mirror image copies
  a human-form worgen as race 1
- CMSG_CHAR_CREATE: optional ZEPF block (uint32 'ZEPF', form, n, look) after ZEPO; a worgen's form 1 look
  is checked against the human CharSections and stored
- CMSG_ALTER_APPEARANCE: in the human form the styles are validated against race 1 and the human look is
  saved at once; a ZEPF block for the form showing sets eye / markings / jewellery / geoset slots
  (also the F-230 barber slots for every race)
- customize / race / faction change with a race or gender change drops the human look

Design follows Medviten's Cataclysm-style altered form (https://github.com/Medviten/wowdecomp-32-bit,
https://github.com/Medviten/WHE-256-bit), used with the author's permission.

